    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Under the assumption that the residual errors are uncorrelated and homoscedastic (i.e., the covariance matrix of the residuals is $ \\sigma_{e}^{2} \\cdot \\mathbf{I} $), the covariance matrix of the elements of b is",
      "source_page": 216,
      "printed_page": 196,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter8:p024:b15"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        163.0,
        1395.0,
        1122.0,
        1514.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
